  "body": "**Theme tokens from SolidCraft:** CamCraft's colours, accents and colour-vision modes come from `solidcraft-theme` and `solidcraft-color`. Those are SolidCraft's token crates, already app-free and pinnable per solidcraft#14251.\n\n**Today:** CamCraft builds its own visuals on `Visuals::dark()` in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme.rs`, with its own `colorvision.rs` and `cvd.rs`.\n\n**Plan:**\n1. Pin both crates by git revision or tag. They aren't on crates.io; ask nateuax or jyviko on Discord which ref to pin.\n2. Install CamCraft's tabs as a `TabTable` with `AccentRamp`s, the way solidcraft#14399 makes tabs host data.\n3. Map CamCraft's colour-vision modes onto the theme crate's.\n\n**Dependency:** this adds a new dependency, so the PR goes to the maintainer (`needs-maintainer`). The crates are Apache-2.0, so their NOTICE is kept in `assets/ui/LICENSES.md`.\n\n**Done means:** the main window, panels and tree draw with SolidCraft's light and dark tokens and tab accents, with light and dark both selectable. The colour-vision tests (`colorvision_tests.rs`) and the structural tests pass. No pixel goldens change in the PR; they're refreshed at the cut.\n\nDepends on #658 (the egui 0.37 bump). Part of #655\n",
